# Consumed by Cloudflare Pages / Netlify (this file is NOT served to visitors).
# The wasm and model filenames never change, so they can be cached forever - which is what
# makes the first photo analysis fast on repeat visits.
#
# NOTE: this file is pure ASCII on purpose. It is parsed by infrastructure, and a parser that
# mishandles multi-byte characters in a comment could silently drop the headers below.
# Keep it ASCII-only, same as the generated robots.txt.

/mediapipe/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin

/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin

# RFC 8288 Link headers for agent discovery.
# Deliberately only relations this site can actually honour:
#   service-doc     -> the methodology / limitations page (our closest thing to API docs)
#   privacy-policy  -> the registered relation for exactly that
#   help            -> where to report a wrong result
#
# We deliberately do NOT advertise api-catalog / service-desc / status, because this site has no
# API. Publishing discovery metadata for endpoints that do not exist is worse for an agent than
# publishing nothing: it would follow the links and fail. See AGENT-READINESS.md.
#
# All values sit on ONE line (a comma-separated list of link-values): repeated same-name headers
# are not guaranteed to be preserved by every static host.
/*
  Link: </how-it-works/>; rel="service-doc", </privacy/>; rel="privacy-policy", </contact/>; rel="help"
